# Booking — Future-commitment worklist (M23-S08, UC-073, UC-077)
# TenantContext populated from X-Tenant-ID / X-Actor-ID headers (set by BFF).
# MANAGER-only on every route. Bulk-only: a single entry is a list of one, and the actions are
# best-effort per entry — a 200 whose `results` says which entries were resolved and which stayed
# OPEN (with the reason as `errorCode`).
#
# Entries are created by deactivating a resource that has future bookings (DELETE /resources/:id in
# resources.http) or by deactivating the staff member behind one.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@exceptionId = {{exceptionId}}
@targetId    = {{targetResourceId}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — the worklist (UC-073)
# Each item carries the affected booking's summary and the advisory alternatives.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### The open worklist, earliest booking first
GET {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions?status=OPEN
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

###

### Every entry, whatever its status
GET {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — resolve one or many entries (UC-077)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### KEEP — the booking stays as it is
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "KEEP",
  "reason": "The customer will use another room"
}

###

### REASSIGN to a chosen resource — same window, time and price untouched
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "REASSIGN",
  "target": { "resourceId": "{{targetId}}" }
}

###

### REASSIGN many at once, each booking to the least-loaded free resource of its type (AUTO)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}", "{{secondExceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "REASSIGN",
  "target": { "mode": "AUTO" }
}

###

### CANCEL — cancels the booking as staff and releases its resource
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "CANCEL",
  "reason": "The room is closed"
}

###

### RESCHEDULE — one entry, an APPROVED booking, applied immediately
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "RESCHEDULE",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — dismiss (UC-077 A2)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### Dismiss entries that need no action
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/dismiss
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "reason": "Already handled by phone"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR PATHS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### 200 with a per-entry failure — an unknown id is BOOKING_EXCEPTION_NOT_FOUND, an entry that is
# already closed is BOOKING_EXCEPTION_ALREADY_RESOLVED, and a target that is busy, inactive, of
# another type or outside the requirement's pool is BOOKING_EXCEPTION_REASSIGN_TARGET_INVALID.
# In every case the entry stays OPEN and the rest of the batch is still resolved.
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["00000000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dead", "{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "KEEP"
}

###

### 400 — REASSIGN needs a target
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "REASSIGN"
}

###

### 400 — RESCHEDULE takes exactly one entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}", "{{secondExceptionId}}"],
  "resolutionType": "RESCHEDULE",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-10-20T13:00:00.000Z"
}

###

### 400 — an empty list of ids (also refused: more than 100, or duplicates)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": [],
  "resolutionType": "KEEP"
}

###

### 400 — dismissing needs a reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/dismiss
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exceptionIds": ["{{exceptionId}}"]
}

###

### 403 — STAFF (non-manager) cannot use the worklist
GET {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 404 — the retired per-id routes no longer exist
POST {{baseUrl}}/scheduling-exceptions/{{exceptionId}}/resolve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionType": "KEEP" }
